= Data leakage (machine learning) — Technical =

== Availability condition ==
Let I_pred denote information legitimately available at prediction time.

A feature/pipeline is leaky when fitting or evaluation uses information outside I_pred in a way that affects the learned predictor or score.

== Common leakage channels ==
<pre>
target-derived feature
future event → past prediction
global preprocessing before split
subject/group overlap
duplicate / near-duplicate overlap
feature selection on test labels
benchmark examples in training
</pre>

== Grouped and temporal data ==
Random row splitting can leak information when rows from the same entity, session, household, device, patient, document, or time series are highly dependent.

Group-aware and temporal splitting can be required.

== Pipeline rule ==
Transformers with fitted state should be trained on the training partition only and then applied to held-out data.

